<section class="hero">
  <h1>Discount, or <em>Premium?</em></h1>
  <div class="hero-subtitle">Bitcoin runs above and below its long-run power law trend &mdash; sometimes far above, sometimes far below.</div>
  <p class="subtitle">This page tells you <em>where in that trend bitcoin sits right now</em> &mdash; and what returning to trend would mean.</p>
</section>

<main class="content-area">

  {% include 'components/tool-framing.njk' %}

  <div class="section-intro dp-prose">
    <p>Most investors think in terms of CAGR &mdash; it is how most equities and other financial instruments grow. Bitcoin is different: perhaps uniquely among major assets, its entire price history has tracked a power law &mdash; a high but declining growth rate along a rising trend, with price oscillating around that trend. So the useful question is not &ldquo;what return does bitcoin give&rdquo; but a two-part one: <strong>where is bitcoin&rsquo;s price relative to trend right now</strong> &mdash; and <strong>if it returns to trend, by when</strong>?</p>
    <p>Below trend, reversion implies an <strong>elevated</strong> near-term CAGR &mdash; the &ldquo;discount&rdquo; case. Above trend, the identical arithmetic implies a depressed or even negative one &mdash; the &ldquo;premium&rdquo; case. Both come out of the same formula with no special-casing.</p>
  </div>

