  <!-- ════════ SOURCES & DISCLOSURES ════════ -->
  <div class="dp-sources">
    <div class="dp-sources-label">Sources &amp; disclosures</div>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>The model.</strong> Every figure is the reference Power Law trend re-expressed in CAGR terms &mdash; no new coefficients, no second model. The trend, the channel, and the credit to Porkopolis Economics for the coefficients all live on <a href="/the-power-law">The Channel</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>A model, not destiny.</strong> The Power Law is an empirical regularity that has held across bitcoin&rsquo;s history. It is not a law of nature and it can break. The <a href="/the-power-law#caveats">caveats</a> set out what would falsify it.</li>
      <li><strong>Reversion is your assumption.</strong> Nothing here predicts that price returns to trend, or when. The page computes the arithmetic consequence of a speed <em>you</em> choose, and shows the never-reverts case alongside it at all times.</li>
      <li><strong>Not an entry signal.</strong> A discount is not a buy signal and a premium is not a sell signal. There are no buy zones on this page by design; for the entry question, see <a href="/wait-or-deploy-now">Wait, or Deploy Now?</a></li>
      <li><strong>Price data.</strong> Live spot from CoinGecko, falling back to the latest monthly sample in the shared series &mdash; labelled as &ldquo;latest monthly data&rdquo; whenever the live fetch does not resolve.</li>
    </ul>
